WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.851
The next morning, the Tornadoes met at the Donovans' tree house.

2
00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:11.772
"We can find the oldest gravestone in the cemetery," said Laura.

3
00:00:11.773 --> 00:00:15.398
"But where will we find the oldest person?"

4
00:00:15.399 --> 00:00:19.042
"Maybe at the Willow Creek Senior Home," said Joy.

5
00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:21.712
"Lots of old people live there."

6
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:27.506
"We can get a calendar of community events at the library," said Carlos.

7
00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:32.159
"But how will we find a town law?" asked Joy.

8
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.760
She looked down at the list and frowned.

9
00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:38.812
"We have less than two weeks to find all this stuff."

10
00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:41.833
"I can help!" said Manny.

11
00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:47.840
"No. You can't," said Carlos. "You're a baby."

12
00:00:47.841 --> 00:00:51.248
"He can count, right?" said Joy.

13
00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:57.412
"We have to count stop signs, mailboxes, and streetlamps on Main Street."

14
00:00:57.413 --> 00:01:01.411
"I can count to a hundred!" said Manny.

15
00:01:01.412 --> 00:01:04.218
"Good enough," said Joy.

16
00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:11.730
Just then a gray cloud drifted through the tree house. Laura coughed.

17
00:01:11.731 --> 00:01:15.422
Carlos sniffed the air.

18
00:01:15.423 --> 00:01:18.569
"I smell smoke," he said.

19
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.545
The Tornadoes looked out of the tree house window.

20
00:01:22.546 --> 00:01:27.283
"Hey, Grandpa!" Joy yelled. "What are you doing?"

21
00:01:27.284 --> 00:01:29.035
Grandpa looked up.

22
00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:31.302
"Oh, hey, kids," he said.

23
00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:33.927
"I'm just burning a few weeds."

24
00:01:33.928 --> 00:01:36.977
He poked at his fire with a stick.

25
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:41.435
A glowing leaf floated up and landed in dry grass.

26
00:01:41.436 --> 00:01:43.172
A flame shot up.

27
00:01:43.173 --> 00:01:48.236
"Oops," said Grandpa and smashed the flame with his boot.

28
00:01:48.237 --> 00:01:51.340
"There goes another one," said Carlos.

29
00:01:51.341 --> 00:01:54.689
Grandpa smashed another little flame.

30
00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:59.486
"And there's one," said Joy. Grandpa stamped again.

31
00:01:59.487 --> 00:02:03.158
Suddenly there were little flames everywhere.

32
00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:09.890
Grandpa was running in a panic, stamping his feet.

33
00:02:09.891 --> 00:02:12.675
"Uh-oh," said Manny.

34
00:02:12.676 --> 00:02:16.320
The kids hurried down the tree house steps.

35
00:02:16.321 --> 00:02:20.529
"Get a bucket from the back porch!" Grandpa yelled.

36
00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.513
The Tornadoes took off.

37
00:02:22.514 --> 00:02:27.884
But by the time they ran back up the hill, the fire was blazing.

38
00:02:27.885 --> 00:02:31.063
Smoke sailed into the sky.

39
00:02:31.064 --> 00:02:35.491
Grandpa grabbed the bucket and dipped it in the pond.

40
00:02:35.492 --> 00:02:40.193
He threw water on the fire, but the fire kept growing.

41
00:02:40.194 --> 00:02:42.932
Then they heard sirens.

42
00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:46.651
"Fire trucks!" shouted Carlos.

43
00:02:46.652 --> 00:02:51.660
The fire chief's truck was in front and the fire engine followed.

44
00:02:51.661 --> 00:02:55.936
They roared up the driveway and across the field.

45
00:02:55.937 --> 00:03:01.070
Three firefighters jumped out and unrolled the fire hose.

46
00:03:01.071 --> 00:03:05.951
"Get back!" the fire chief called to Grandpa and the kids.

47
00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:10.449
Water whooshed out of the hose and onto the fire.

48
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:16.338
Soon there was just a circle of wet, black grass where the fire had been.

49
00:03:16.339 --> 00:03:19.942
"What happened here?" asked the fire chief.

50
00:03:19.943 --> 00:03:22.139
Her name was Rita Carlson.

51
00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.120
She had been a Willow Creek firefighter for 15 years.

52
00:03:27.121 --> 00:03:32.015
"Well," said Grandpa, "I was just burning a few weeds.

53
00:03:32.016 --> 00:03:34.710
Then the fire went everywhere.

54
00:03:34.711 --> 00:03:37.602
When the kids got here with the bucket—"

55
00:03:37.603 --> 00:03:40.871
Chief Carlson interrupted Grandpa.

56
00:03:40.872 --> 00:03:46.082
"So you didn't have anything ready to control your fire?" she asked.

57
00:03:46.083 --> 00:03:49.612
"I guess not," said Grandpa.

58
00:03:49.613 --> 00:03:51.783
The fire chief frowned.

59
00:03:51.784 --> 00:03:56.348
"May I see your burning permit, Mr. Donovan?"

60
00:03:56.349 --> 00:04:00.107
"Burning permit?" said Grandpa.

61
00:04:00.108 --> 00:04:02.406
Chief Carlson sighed.

62
00:04:02.407 --> 00:04:10.097
"Mr. Donovan, Willow Creek's burning law requires you to get a burning permit before starting a fire.

63
00:04:10.098 --> 00:04:12.411
You have broken that law."

64
00:04:12.412 --> 00:04:15.633
"Hooray!" cried Joy.

65
00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:18.316
Everyone stared at Joy.

66
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:22.466
"That's just what we're looking for!" she explained.

67
00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.875
"A law for our scavenger hunt!

68
00:04:24.876 --> 00:04:28.601
Do you have a copy of the burning law, Chief Carlson?"

69
00:04:28.602 --> 00:04:34.021
"Oh! We need a list of fire-safety tips too," said Laura.

70
00:04:34.022 --> 00:04:37.360
"No problem," said Chief Carlson.

71
00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:39.696
"I have both of those things in my truck.

72
00:04:39.697 --> 00:04:43.966
And for you, Mr. Donovan, I have a fine."

73
00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:48.188
Grandpa frowned. But the Tornadoes cheered.

74
00:04:48.189 --> 00:04:54.787
The fire trucks were just leaving when Katie came racing down Blackberry Road on her bike.

75
00:04:54.788 --> 00:04:58.203
"Here comes an Earthworm!" said Carlos.

76
00:04:58.204 --> 00:05:00.357
"Don't tell her what we found!"

77
00:05:00.358 --> 00:05:06.285
The Tornadoes laughed and put two check marks on their list.

